notes:
Formed as {四|よん} × {千|せん}. Always {よんせん}, never しせん — {し} is avoided here because it is a homophone of {死|し} (death) and because {よん} is the default counting form before counters.

SOUND CHANGES IN THE THOUSANDS:
- {三千|さんぜん}: 3,000 — {せん} voices to {ぜん}
- {八千|はっせん}: 8,000 — {はち} shortens to {はっ}
- {一千|いっせん}: 1,000 — {いち} shortens to {いっ}
- {四千|よんせん}, {五千|ごせん}, {六千|ろくせん}, {七千|ななせん}, {九千|きゅうせん}: regular

COMMON EXPRESSIONS:
- {四千|よんせん}{円|えん}: four thousand yen
- {四千|よんせん}{人|にん}: four thousand people
- {四千|よんせん}メートル{級|きゅう}: in the four-thousand-metre class (of mountains)
